WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.942
The core contribution is a general dual-based
formulation of Kernel PCA built on the dualization

00:00:04.022 --> 00:00:07.963
of a difference of convex functions.

00:00:08.043 --> 00:00:11.985
This formulation does two things at once.

00:00:12.065 --> 00:00:16.007
First, it turns the problem into one over a
finite-dimensional dual matrix,

00:00:16.087 --> 00:00:20.028
which can be solved with efficient gradient-based
methods and avoids the expensive singular value decomposition,

00:00:20.108 --> 00:00:24.050
even when the feature space is infinite-dimensional.

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:28.072
Second,

00:00:28.152 --> 00:00:32.093
it makes the objective modular: by choosing
objectives expressible as Moreau envelopes,

00:00:32.173 --> 00:00:36.115
the same framework promotes robustness or sparsity
without leaving the dual picture.

00:00:36.195 --> 00:00:40.137
The authors supply the supporting theory,

00:00:40.217 --> 00:00:44.158
concrete L-BFGS and difference-of-convex algorithms,

00:00:44.238 --> 00:00:48.180
and the proximal operators needed to make the
robust and sparse cases practical.
